      "description": "Day 70 of 100 Days of Learning AI 👉 Stop Single-Vendor Lock-in: Go Model-Agnostic! 💡\nHardcoding OpenAI proprietary API calls throughout your entire codebase is dangerous. When prices change or competitors leap ahead, you're trapped.\n\n🧠 KEY TAKEAWAYS:\n- Vendor lock-in leaves you vulnerable to sudden price spikes, outages, and policy shifts.\n- Use open abstraction layers (LiteLLM, LangChain, OpenRouter) to route requests.\n- Swap between Claude 3.5 Sonnet, GPT-4o, and DeepSeek with a single config flag.\n- Enables automatic failover routing when a cloud provider suffers an outage.\n\n🔄 Never marry a single model provider; stay architecturally agile and model-agnostic.\n\n───────────────\n🎯 ABOUT THIS SERIES:\nWelcome to Day 70 of 100 Days of Learning AI (Sigma Byte series) with Sarav! Every day in under 45 seconds, we break down high-IQ Artificial Intelligence concepts into clear, practical intuition for creators, developers, and enterprise leaders.\n\n👇 TODAY'S QUESTION:\nIs your codebase hardcoded to one LLM provider, or are you model-agnostic? Drop 'LOCKED-IN' or 'AGNOSTIC' below!\nDrop your thoughts in the comments below! 💬\n\n🔔 SUBSCRIBE to @iamsaravofficial to master AI one byte at a time!\n📌 SAVE the '100 Days of Learning AI' playlist to never miss an episode.\n🌐 Explore projects & architecture: https://iamsaravofficial.com/ai\n───────────────\n\n#shorts #vendorlockin #ai #artificialintelligence #promptengineering #aitools #learnai #sigmabyte #saravxai #100daysofai #machinelearning #techtips",
