      "description": "Day 72 of 100 Days of Learning AI 👉 Stop Full Retraining: Fine-Tune 1% With LoRA! 💡\nRetraining a 70-Billion parameter model requires a million-dollar GPU cluster. LoRA freezes the base model and trains tiny adapter matrices.\n\n🧠 KEY TAKEAWAYS:\n- Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) decomposes weight updates into two smaller low-rank matrices.\n- Freezes 99% of base model weights, training only 1% of parameters.\n- Runs on a single consumer GPU (like an RTX 3090 or RTX 4090) in a few hours.\n- Swap tiny 50MB LoRA adapter files dynamically to switch between legal, medical, or coding modes.\n\n🔄 Don't move the entire mountain; train tiny 1% LoRA adapters for $5.\n\n───────────────\n🎯 ABOUT THIS SERIES:\nWelcome to Day 72 of 100 Days of Learning AI (Sigma Byte series) with Sarav! Every day in under 45 seconds, we break down high-IQ Artificial Intelligence concepts into clear, practical intuition for creators, developers, and enterprise leaders.\n\n👇 TODAY'S QUESTION:\nHave you trained a LoRA adapter for Stable Diffusion or an LLM? Drop 'YES' or 'WANT TO LEARN' below!\nDrop your thoughts in the comments below! 💬\n\n🔔 SUBSCRIBE to @iamsaravofficial to master AI one byte at a time!\n📌 SAVE the '100 Days of Learning AI' playlist to never miss an episode.\n🌐 Explore projects & architecture: https://iamsaravofficial.com/ai\n───────────────\n\n#shorts #lora #ai #artificialintelligence #promptengineering #aitools #learnai #sigmabyte #saravxai #100daysofai #machinelearning #techtips",
