      "title": "(Day 73/100) Stop Burning Cloud VRAM: Quantize Models to 4-Bit Int #shorts #ai",
      "description": "Day 73 of 100 Days of Learning AI 👉 Stop Burning VRAM: Quantize AI to 4-Bit Int! 💡\nWhy pay for 80GB enterprise GPUs when you can run state-of-the-art models on a laptop? Quantization compresses 16-bit floats down to 4-bit integers.\n\n🧠 KEY TAKEAWAYS:\n- Models natively train in 16-bit floating point precision (FP16), consuming huge VRAM.\n- Quantization (INT8, INT4, AWQ, GGUF) rounds weights down with under 1% accuracy loss.\n- Shrinks a 14GB model down to 4.5GB, fitting directly onto consumer laptops and phones.\n- Massively accelerates token generation speed while slashing inference power draw.\n\n🔄 Compress the precision, preserve the intelligence; run frontier AI locally.\n\n───────────────\n🎯 ABOUT THIS SERIES:\nWelcome to Day 73 of 100 Days of Learning AI (Sigma Byte series) with Sarav! Every day in under 45 seconds, we break down high-IQ Artificial Intelligence concepts into clear, practical intuition for creators, developers, and enterprise leaders.\n\n👇 TODAY'S QUESTION:\nDo you run quantized models (GGUF, EXL2) locally on your PC or Mac? Drop 'LOCAL GGUF' or 'CLOUD APIS' below!\nDrop your thoughts in the comments below! 💬\n\n🔔 SUBSCRIBE to @iamsaravofficial to master AI one byte at a time!\n📌 SAVE the '100 Days of Learning AI' playlist to never miss an episode.\n🌐 Explore projects & architecture: https://iamsaravofficial.com/ai\n───────────────\n\n#shorts #quantization #ai #artificialintelligence #promptengineering #aitools #learnai #sigmabyte #saravxai #100daysofai #machinelearning #techtips",
