      "description": "Day 74 of 100 Days of Learning AI 👉 Stop Activating 70B Weights: Use MoE Routing! 💡\nWhy wake up 100% of an AI model to answer a simple math question? Mixture of Experts (MoE) routes each token to specialized sub-networks.\n\n🧠 KEY TAKEAWAYS:\n- Dense models activate every single parameter for every token generated.\n- MoE architectures (Mixtral, GPT-4, Grok) divide parameters into specialized expert networks.\n- A learned gating router selects the top-2 experts per token on the fly.\n- Delivers 70B-grade intelligence with the blazing speed and compute cost of a 14B model.\n\n🔄 Don't burn energy waking the whole brain; route every token to the specialist.\n\n───────────────\n🎯 ABOUT THIS SERIES:\nWelcome to Day 74 of 100 Days of Learning AI (Sigma Byte series) with Sarav! Every day in under 45 seconds, we break down high-IQ Artificial Intelligence concepts into clear, practical intuition for creators, developers, and enterprise leaders.\n\n👇 TODAY'S QUESTION:\nDid you know GPT-4 is widely believed to be an 8x220B Mixture of Experts model? Drop 'YES' or 'REALLY?' below!\nDrop your thoughts in the comments below! 💬\n\n🔔 SUBSCRIBE to @iamsaravofficial to master AI one byte at a time!\n📌 SAVE the '100 Days of Learning AI' playlist to never miss an episode.\n🌐 Explore projects & architecture: https://iamsaravofficial.com/ai\n───────────────\n\n#shorts #mixtureofexperts #ai #artificialintelligence #promptengineering #aitools #learnai #sigmabyte #saravxai #100daysofai #machinelearning #techtips",
