      "description": "Day 77 of 100 Days of Learning AI 👉 Stop Confusing AI Stages: Pretrain vs Instruct! 💡\nBase models and Chat models are completely different beasts. Pretraining builds universal knowledge; instruction tuning teaches conversational obedience.\n\n🧠 KEY TAKEAWAYS:\n- Stage 1 (Pretraining): Self-supervised learning on trillions of web tokens predicting next words.\n- Base models are raw statistical predictors—if you ask a question, they might generate more questions.\n- Stage 2 (Supervised Fine-Tuning / SFT): Trains the model to follow instructions and answer queries.\n- Understanding this separation is crucial for fine-tuning, steering, and architectural evaluation.\n\n🔄 Pretraining creates raw encyclopedic memory; instruction tuning teaches it to speak.\n\n───────────────\n🎯 ABOUT THIS SERIES:\nWelcome to Day 77 of 100 Days of Learning AI (Sigma Byte series) with Sarav! Every day in under 45 seconds, we break down high-IQ Artificial Intelligence concepts into clear, practical intuition for creators, developers, and enterprise leaders.\n\n👇 TODAY'S QUESTION:\nHave you ever accidentally used a base model (like Llama-3-8B-Base) and wondered why it wouldn't chat? Drop 'YES' or 'NEVER' below!\nDrop your thoughts in the comments below! 💬\n\n🔔 SUBSCRIBE to @iamsaravofficial to master AI one byte at a time!\n📌 SAVE the '100 Days of Learning AI' playlist to never miss an episode.\n🌐 Explore projects & architecture: https://iamsaravofficial.com/ai\n───────────────\n\n#shorts #pretraining #ai #artificialintelligence #promptengineering #aitools #learnai #sigmabyte #saravxai #100daysofai #machinelearning #techtips",
