      "filename": "SIGMA_BYTE_88_How_AI_Apps_Got_Cheaper_A.mp4",
      "title": "(Day 88/100) Stop Paying Full Price for Static Tokens: Enable Caching #shorts #ai",
      "description": "Day 88 of 100 Days of Learning AI 👉 Stop Paying for Static Tokens: Use Cache Reads! 💡\nSending the same 50-page system prompt or company handbook on every API call is throwing money away. Prompt caching cuts read costs by up to 90%.\n\n🧠 KEY TAKEAWAYS:\n- Frontier APIs (Anthropic, Gemini, OpenAI) cache token prefix activations in server memory.\n- Subsequent requests reading cached prefixes receive an 80% to 90% discount on input tokens.\n- Slashes time-to-first-token (TTFT) latency by avoiding redundant neural forward passes.\n- A mandatory architectural optimization for multi-turn chat and heavy enterprise RAG.\n\n🔄 Cache the static prefix once; read it thousands of times for 90% off.\n\n───────────────\n🎯 ABOUT THIS SERIES:\nWelcome to Day 88 of 100 Days of Learning AI (Sigma Byte series) with Sarav! Every day in under 45 seconds, we break down high-IQ Artificial Intelligence concepts into clear, practical intuition for creators, developers, and enterprise leaders.\n\n👇 TODAY'S QUESTION:\nAre you using prompt caching in your Claude or Gemini API implementations? Drop 'CACHING' or 'MISSING OUT' below!\nDrop your thoughts in the comments below! 💬\n\n🔔 SUBSCRIBE to @iamsaravofficial to master AI one byte at a time!\n📌 SAVE the '100 Days of Learning AI' playlist to never miss an episode.\n🌐 Explore projects & architecture: https://iamsaravofficial.com/ai\n───────────────\n\n#shorts #contextcaching #ai #artificialintelligence #promptengineering #aitools #learnai #sigmabyte #saravxai #100daysofai #machinelearning #techtips",
