      "caption": "Across twenty feet of strangers, her eyes snapped to his.\n\nDAY 27 OF 30 • ACT IV: THE UNDENIABLE US – MUNICH & HOME WAS YOU - The Bavarian Crowd\n\nTheresienwiese roared with brass music and laughter. Inside the Paulaner tent, overflowing one-litre beer steins clinked above wooden tables, Bavarian cheers drowning the world. Sid lifted his glass, nursing a hazy buzz amidst his colleagues. Then, the universe froze. She turned her head, tossing dark curls over her shoulder with an unmistakably familiar tilt. \"Isha?\"\n\nCutting across the lantern-lit aisle in an elegant woolen trench coat stood a woman holding a warm pretzel. The stein slipped an inch in Sid’s hand. he breathed. Across twenty feet of singing strangers, her amber eyes snapped to his.\n\nThis is Day 27 of SIDISHA - Home Was You\nA 30-Day Drabble Collection by Nalkudil Studio\nOne memory. One spark. Every morning 10:15 AM IST.\n\n🔊 Sound on: Chasing Cars (Acoustic) Â· Snow Patrol / Paulaner Tent Vibe\n\nRead with illustrations on blog - link in bio\nFree 30-Day Booklet: iamsaravofficial.com/book-club\n\nWhat would you do if you locked eyes with your high school love in a crowded foreign city? 👇\n\n#sidisha #homewasyou #drabble #lovestory #nalkudilstudio",
